    "text": "Dividend Mutual Fund List: A dividend mutual fund is one of the MF categories where the focus is mainly on investing in regular, dividend-paying stocks. These companies are usually well-established, financially stable, and generate consistent profits. While investing in a dividend mutual fund, investors hope to get steady returns through dividends, along with long-term capital growth. Predominantly invest in dividend-yielding stocks, with at least 65% in stocks in the folio as per Sebi guideline.",
